    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSELLING PROCESS CONCLUDED 28th August. \n\n \n\nREA MURPHY is delighted to bring this substantial detached family home to the market move-in ready and competitively priced to sell. Offering generous four-bedroom accommodation with exciting potential to change and personalise, 5 Deerpark View is a property that genuinely rewards viewing. \n\nSituated in the compact, well-established development of Deerpark View just 29 homes in total this detached four-bedroom property occupies a particularly appealing position at the end of a quiet cul-de-sac. The result is noticeably less traffic, an additional play area right beside the house, and a real sense of privacy and seclusion that is hard to find in modern estates. The property comes with ample off-street parking and an impressively wide side entrance, which would lend itself naturally to a car port, particularly if the integrated garage were converted to additional living accommodation. To the rear, the garden has been extended beyond its original footprint, enjoys a sunny south-facing aspect, and is both fully enclosed and exceptionally private a wonderful space for families. A sizable concrete block garden shed adds further practical value.\n\nInternally, the property is presented to a very acceptable standard for immediate occupancy, while also offering the kind of versatility that allows a new owner to put their own stamp on the property over time. A garage conversion would unlock significant additional living or 5th Bedroom space, and the En Suite - ready to be fitted to taste offers scope to create a genuinely impressive principal bedroom suite. Whether a dedicated home office is needed downstairs, upstairs, or in the garden, this layout accommodates each option with ease.\n\nBaltinglass is a thriving and self-sufficient market town of approximately 2,300 residents, with an excellent range of everyday amenities: GP practices, two pharmacies, supermarket, convenience stores, primary and secondary schools, pre-school crches, and a broad variety of sporting clubs and leisure facilities. Number 5 Deerpark View is within comfortable walking distance of the town centre, the schools, and all local clubs making it an ideal permanent family home in a settled, friendly community.\n\nVIEWING THIS PROPERTY IS STRONGLY RECOMMENDED. \n\n \n\nACCOMMODATION:\n\nEntrance Hall with understairs storage.\n\nLounge.\n\nKitchen / Living / Dining area.\n\nUtility area with W.C.\n\nGarage.\n\n1st Floor:\n\nSpacious landing area.\n\n4 double bedrooms fitted wardrobes.\n\nEn Suite - to be fitted out.\n\nBathroom.\n\nOUTSIDE:\n\nOn-site parking to the front.\n\nPedestrian and vehicular side entrances to the rear garden.\n\nEnclosed, extra-large rear garden.\n\nConcrete block garden shed.\n\nTRANSPORT:\n\n132 Bus Route to Dublin City Centre via Tallaght Hospital. \n\n885 Bus Route to Naas and Sallins Train Station.\n\nKavanagh bus to Carlow Town and The Institute of Technology, Carlow.\n\nSERVICES:\n\nOil fired central heating. Excellent broadband available.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
